WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.320
Good morning, John.

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:02.679
In my last video I complained.

00:00:02.679 --> 00:00:07.560
And my first rant, of all my rants, was ranting
about ranting and why people enjoy ranting

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:11.560
and listening to rants so much when the world
is actually full of pretty cool stuff.

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:14.940
So in this video, to counteract that, I'm
going to be sharing fifteen of my very favorite

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:16.610
feelings in the world ever.

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:17.670
It's not gonna be super funny.

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:21.380
It's not gonna fire your dopamine receptors
in the same way that getting all jazzed up

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:24.400
and angry will, and it might not even be like
so relatable.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.630
Instead of those things, I'm just going for
honest.

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:27.920
So, my favorite feelings.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:31.930
Seeing two people that you really like get
married to each other and everybody in their

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:37.280
lives who love them have come together to
just be unironically sappy about how adorable

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:38.989
their faces are for a day.

00:00:38.989 --> 00:00:41.809
Hanging out with an old friend for the first
time in years, and you've forgotten a lot

00:00:41.809 --> 00:00:44.870
of the things about them, and you're hanging
out, and, you, they're just great!

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:46.699
And you're like "I like you so much!

00:00:46.699 --> 00:00:48.170
We get along really well!

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:51.850
That's probably why we used to hang out like
every day."

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:56.819
Figuring out something super complicated like,
for example, uuuuuuuhhhhhh this thing.

00:00:56.819 --> 00:00:58.629
It just sits there on the floor now.

00:00:58.629 --> 00:01:02.239
That's not one of my favorite feelings: having
just junk lying around.

00:01:02.239 --> 00:01:06.630
But the complicated thing can be like a real
problem that I face in my life or some contrived

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:08.280
thing from a book or a video game.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.470
That moment of figuring it out is so great!

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.259
I guess, somewhat relatedly, just getting
better at stuff.

00:01:13.259 --> 00:01:16.810
Like that moment when you realize that you
can now do something very easily that a year

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:19.390
ago would have been unthinkably difficult.

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:24.170
Having the power to feel comfortable being
me and having society recognize you for your

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:28.820
strengths is pretty rare and pretty rad and
I have that right now.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:33.109
And I never want to take it for granted and
if I don't have it anymore, which is certainly

00:01:33.109 --> 00:01:35.491
possible, I do not want to be bitter about
it.

00:01:35.491 --> 00:01:39.140
Having someone you respect tell you that they
respect you - mh.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:40.520
So good.

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:45.530
When you're reading a book and there are like
35 different weird plot threads that seem

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:49.939
to have nothing to do with each other until
one thing is removed or added to the equation

00:01:49.939 --> 00:01:55.040
and suddenly they all form together this magnificent
tapestry of everything and it all fits together

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:57.039
and you're like "What just happened?!"

00:01:57.039 --> 00:01:58.350
Love that, I love that a lot.

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:00.210
Doing something scary and having it go really
well.

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:01.890
Taking a hot shower in the dead of winter.

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:03.859
Smelling the first iris of the year.

00:02:03.859 --> 00:02:05.109
Not like of an eyeball.

00:02:05.109 --> 00:02:07.369
An iris is a plant, if you don't have those.

00:02:07.369 --> 00:02:09.410
Don't sniff each other's eyeballs.

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:11.430
Unless it's consensual...

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:16.250
Maybe the best feeling of all feelings, that
I've ever had, is opening up and letting somebody

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:18.720
that you love see all your broken bits.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:21.900
And then they're like "I don't mind, those
are pretty cool.

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:23.150
Here are mine, too."

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:25.140
And you're like "Yeah, no, I like those.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:26.140
Those are cool.

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:27.140
That's fine.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:28.160
We should hold, and hug."

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:31.271
Knowing that yes, this person that you love
loves you back and you can trust that and

00:02:31.271 --> 00:02:33.110
you can know it forever.

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:34.210
Yeah!

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:38.390
Less good than that, but still very good,
is when the cat is like "Don't, you, stop

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:39.390
moving.

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:40.390
I need to cuddle you."

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:44.310
Another amazing feeling: learning things that
help me understand the world better.

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:47.590
Also helping people learn things that help
them understand the world better.

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:51.811
I'm gonna finish this list off with a feeling
that I thought would feel really good, but

00:02:51.811 --> 00:02:56.400
now that I've experienced it a few times clearly
does not: watching bad people, who have done

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:00.560
bad things to me or to other people and I've
seen it happen, watching those people fail

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:05.010
or self-destruct or have bad things happen
to them, it never feels good.

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:10.840
Like watching bad people is sad when they're
successful and when they're failing.

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:12.870
It doesn't matter what's happening.

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:14.180
It's always just sad.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:18.110
John, I'm gonna be honest, I found this video
surprisingly hard to make.

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:22.690
Even in a little corner of the internet that
we inhabit that is a very open and honest

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:23.690
and authentic place.

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:26.200
It was difficult to just share things that
I like.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:27.200
I don't know why.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:30.230
If it's self-consciousness or if it's like
I'm afraid that I'm bragging that I, like,

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:33.850
enjoy things in my life, which is, why would
you feel that way?

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:34.850
I don't know.

00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:39.370
Apparently it's more fun to complain than
to appreciate but probably not better for

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:41.050
a person or the world in the long term.

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:44.040
So I know some of the things above were, like,
probably things that everybody agrees on and

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:45.350
some were very specific to me.

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:50.380
But I'd like to know in the comments if you
just want to open up and tell everybody else

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:53.020
some of your favorite feelings that would
be great.

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:56.300
And also if you want to open up about some
of your hang ups to consenting strangers,

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:57.670
probably down there as well.

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:59.069
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

